review_comment:
Phase 2 extraction lacks proper rollback on failure. If `zf.extract()` raises an exception after successfully extracting some members (e.g., disk full, permission denied), the catch-all at line 2353 will yield an ErrorMessage but leave partial extracts on disk, violating the validate-then-extract all-or-nothing semantics. Consider wrapping Phase 2 in its own try-except that cleans up `root_abs` on any extraction failure before re-raising or yielding the error.
```suggestion
        try:
            os.makedirs(root_abs, exist_ok=True)
            for member in members:
                zf.extract(member, root_abs)
        except Exception as e:
            # Best-effort rollback: remove any partially extracted contents.
            try:
                shutil.rmtree(root_abs)
            except Exception:
                # Ignore rollback errors; the original extraction error is primary.
                pass
            yield ErrorMessage(filename, f"Extraction error: {e}")
            return
```

[nitpick] The `open_datafile` function hardcodes the encoding as "utf-8". While this is appropriate for the current use cases (all files being loaded are UTF-8 encoded), it would be more flexible to make encoding a parameter with a default value of "utf-8" to allow for potential future use cases with different encodings.

Consider:
```python
def open_datafile(path, file_name, encoding="utf-8"):
    # Use .join() to reach the file regardless of zip/real FS.
    return path.join(file_name).open(encoding=encoding)
```
```suggestion
def open_datafile(path, file_name, encoding="utf-8"):
    # Use .join() to reach the file regardless of zip/real FS.
    return path.join(file_name).open(encoding=encoding)
```

