Potential bug: If `corpus-id` is missing from a qrels sample, `corpus_ids` will be `None`, which will cause `isinstance(corpus_ids, list)` to return False, and then `qrels_mapping[sample["query-id"]].add(corpus_ids)` will add `None` to the set instead of skipping or raising an error. Consider adding explicit `None` handling:
```python
corpus_ids = sample.get("corpus-id")
if corpus_ids is None:
    continue  # or raise ValueError with a clear message
if sample["query-id"] not in qrels_mapping:
    qrels_mapping[sample["query-id"]] = set()
if isinstance(corpus_ids, list):
    qrels_mapping[sample["query-id"]].update(corpus_ids)
else:
    qrels_mapping[sample["query-id"]].add(corpus_ids)
```

